       fhir:target ( [
         fhir:code [ fhir:v "Consent.provision.securityLabel" ] ;
         fhir:display [ fhir:v "Consent.provision.securityLabel" ] ;
         fhir:equivalence [ fhir:v "equivalent" ] ;
         fhir:comment [ fhir:v "Element `Consent.provision.securityLabel` is mapped to FHIR R4 element `Consent.provision.securityLabel` as `Equivalent`.\nIf the consent specifies a security label of \"R\" then it applies to all resources that are labeled \"R\" or lower. E.g. for Confidentiality, it's a high water mark. For other kinds of security labels, subsumption logic applies. When the purpose of use tag is on the data, access request purpose of use shall not conflict." ]
